cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software corpus, please cite it as below."
title: "Buddhist and Comparative Asian Logic Formalizations"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/takuya50/buddhist-comparative-logic"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22851717"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked formalizations of Buddhist and comparative Asian logic in
  Lean 4 and Isabelle/HOL. The Heart Sutra is one case study: its
  Isabelle session formalizes a project-adopted 262-character received witness
  of the Xuanzang-attributed text, with manually documented statement-level
  correspondence to selected Lean 4 definitions and results, not a verified
  cross-foundational translation. The source repository is public.
  The shared logical layer compares classical logic, Belnap-Dunn
  first-degree entailment, and Priest's five-valued semantics. Lean extensions
  give bounded proof interfaces and countermodels for Madhyamaka, Buddhist
  epistemology, Yogacara, and selected comparative Asian traditions. The
  historical modules expose their assumptions and are described as modern
  reconstructions unless a passage-level alignment is recorded; the project
  does not assert the truth of a doctrine or a uniquely correct reading.
authors:
